  "summary": "Recent preprints automate cryo-EM model building and density-based hit detection using LLM agents and differentiable reconstruction models.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is the move from manual, sequential structure workflows toward automated, density-aware computation. CryoPilot uses two LLM agents to select CryoSPARC jobs adaptively and validate atomic models across nine public datasets. End2EndPtychoSPA instead fits a 3D potential and particle poses jointly to 4D-STEM data through a differentiable multislice model, reporting resolution gains over sequential reconstruction. On the hit-identification side, FoXSight applies Difference-of-Gaussian filtering to multi-reference subtraction maps to recover recurring ligand-bound density in crystallographic fragment screens, while Astex-Faro flags significant deviations in cryo-EM maps against a reference ensemble and introduces an FSCoh consistency metric. PHENOMS addresses a separate analysis problem, Rust-accelerated extraction of backbone hydrogen-bond networks from MD trajectories linked to HDX-MS.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-05"
}
